Feature: Create invoice
  In order to bill a customer for the products they ordered
  As a user of the invoicing module
  I need to create a draft invoice with the customer's details and product lines

  Rules:
  - An invoice is always created in "draft" status
  - The invoice ID is generated by the system
  - An invoice can be created without product lines
  - Customer name and a valid customer email are required
  - Each product line needs a product name, and a quantity and unit price that are positive integers
  - A line's total unit price is quantity x unit price; the invoice's total price is the sum of the lines' totals
  - An invalid request creates nothing

  # Happy paths

  Scenario: Creating an invoice without product lines
    When I create an invoice for customer "Jane Doe" with email "jane.doe@example.com"
    Then the invoice should be created
    And the invoice should have a generated ID
    And the invoice status should be "draft"
    And the invoice customer name should be "Jane Doe"
    And the invoice customer email should be "jane.doe@example.com"
    And the invoice should have no product lines
    And the invoice total price should be 0

  Scenario: Creating an invoice with product lines
    When I create an invoice for customer "Jane Doe" with email "jane.doe@example.com" and product lines:
      | product name | quantity | unit price |
      | Keyboard     | 2        | 150        |
      | Mouse        | 3        | 10         |
    Then the invoice should be created
    And the invoice status should be "draft"
    And the invoice should have the following product lines:
      | product name | quantity | unit price | total unit price |
      | Keyboard     | 2        | 150        | 300              |
      | Mouse        | 3        | 10         | 30               |
    And the invoice total price should be 330

  Scenario: Creating an invoice with a single unit of a product
    When I create an invoice for customer "Jane Doe" with email "jane.doe@example.com" and product lines:
      | product name | quantity | unit price |
      | Cable        | 1        | 1          |
    Then the invoice should be created
    And the invoice total price should be 1

  Scenario: Each created invoice gets its own ID
    When I create an invoice for customer "Jane Doe" with email "jane.doe@example.com"
    And I create an invoice for customer "John Smith" with email "john.smith@example.com"
    Then there should be 2 invoices
    And the invoices should have different IDs

  # Sad paths: customer details

  Scenario: The customer name is required
    When I create an invoice for customer "" with email "jane.doe@example.com"
    Then the invoice should not be created
    And I should be told that "customer name" is invalid
    And there should be 0 invoices

  Scenario: The customer name cannot consist of whitespace only
    When I create an invoice for customer "   " with email "jane.doe@example.com"
    Then the invoice should not be created
    And I should be told that "customer name" is invalid
    And there should be 0 invoices

  Scenario Outline: The customer email must be a valid email address
    When I create an invoice for customer "Jane Doe" with email "<email>"
    Then the invoice should not be created
    And I should be told that "customer email" is invalid
    And there should be 0 invoices

    Examples:
      | email            |
      |                  |
      | jane.doe         |
      | jane.doe@        |
      | @example.com     |
      | jane doe@ex.com  |

  # Sad paths: product lines

  Scenario: A product line must have a product name
    When I create an invoice for customer "Jane Doe" with email "jane.doe@example.com" and product lines:
      | product name | quantity | unit price |
      |              | 1        | 100        |
    Then the invoice should not be created
    And I should be told that "product name" of product line 1 is invalid
    And there should be 0 invoices

  Scenario Outline: A product line quantity must be a positive integer
    When I create an invoice for customer "Jane Doe" with email "jane.doe@example.com" and product lines:
      | product name | quantity   | unit price |
      | Keyboard     | <quantity> | 150        |
    Then the invoice should not be created
    And I should be told that "quantity" of product line 1 is invalid
    And there should be 0 invoices

    Examples:
      | quantity |
      | 0        |
      | -1       |

    # Values that are not integers cannot even be put into a use case request
    @api_only
    Examples:
      | quantity |
      | 1.5      |
      | two      |
      |          |

  Scenario Outline: A product line unit price must be a positive integer
    When I create an invoice for customer "Jane Doe" with email "jane.doe@example.com" and product lines:
      | product name | quantity | unit price   |
      | Keyboard     | 2        | <unit price> |
    Then the invoice should not be created
    And I should be told that "unit price" of product line 1 is invalid
    And there should be 0 invoices

    Examples:
      | unit price |
      | 0          |
      | -150       |

    # Values that are not integers cannot even be put into a use case request
    @api_only
    Examples:
      | unit price |
      | 1.99       |
      | free       |
      |            |

  Scenario: One invalid product line rejects the whole invoice
    When I create an invoice for customer "Jane Doe" with email "jane.doe@example.com" and product lines:
      | product name | quantity | unit price |
      | Keyboard     | 2        | 150        |
      | Mouse        | 0        | 10         |
    Then the invoice should not be created
    And I should be told that "quantity" of product line 2 is invalid
    And there should be 0 invoices

  Scenario: The total unit price cannot be supplied by the caller
    When I create an invoice for customer "Jane Doe" with email "jane.doe@example.com" and product lines:
      | product name | quantity | unit price | total unit price |
      | Keyboard     | 2        | 150        | 1                |
    Then the invoice should be created
    And the invoice should have the following product lines:
      | product name | quantity | unit price | total unit price |
      | Keyboard     | 2        | 150        | 300              |
    And the invoice total price should be 300

  Scenario: All validation problems are reported at once
    When I create an invoice for customer "" with email "jane.doe" and product lines:
      | product name | quantity | unit price |
      | Keyboard     | 0        | -1         |
    Then the invoice should not be created
    And I should be told that "customer name" is invalid
    And I should be told that "customer email" is invalid
    And I should be told that "quantity" of product line 1 is invalid
    And I should be told that "unit price" of product line 1 is invalid
    And there should be 0 invoices
